{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLHxnvH4JLnvZaYWyYRP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I made two small changes to `sympy/printing/latex.py`. The two examples from the issue already printed correctly on this checkout before I touched anything:\n- `exp(-x)*log(x)` with `x` positive gives `e^{- x} \\log{\\left (x \\right )}`\n- `1/(x + y)/2` gives `\\frac{1}{2 \\left(x + y\\right)}`\n\nWhile comparing more expressions against the pretty printer, I found a real bug in the same area: `latex(Mul(x, Pow(1, -1, evaluate=False), evaluate=False))` recursed forever and crashed.\n\n**Changes:**\n1. **The crash:** in `_print_Mul`, an expression whose only denominator is an unevaluated `1**-1` no longer takes the branch that calls back into itself. It now prints as a fraction, `\\frac{x}{1}`. I also added `Pow` to the imports.\n2. **Brackets:** `_needs_mul_brackets` now brackets any factor that binds more loosely than multiplication, using the same precedence rules as the pretty printer. Before, it only checked for sums and relations explicitly. The explicit checks for relations and negative products are kept.\n\n**Tests:** in `sympy/printing/tests/test_latex.py`, 104 pass and 3 fail. The same 3 failed before my change: `test_latex_symbols_failing`, `test_builtin_without_args_mismatched_names` and `test_issue_8470`. They come from an incompatibility between the Python 3.9 environment and this older SymPy, for example `ValueError: Name node can't be used with 'False' constant` in the parser. I didn't run the pretty-printer tests because that code wasn't changed.\n\n**One remaining difference I left alone:** `(x+y)**(-x)/3` prints in LaTeX as `\\frac{1}{3} \\left(x + y\\right)^{- x}`, while the pretty printer shows a single fraction over 3. That comes from the existing `long_frac_ratio` setting, which deliberately splits long numerators."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1272,"cache_read_input_tokens":31454,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1272},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"16c77b00-f423-46f2-b995-3e98d214f0ad","uuid":"92cd0791-ed39-4dd0-b6ec-f69a633fc214","timestamp":"2026-11-23T17:58:10.224Z","request_id":"req_011ChLHxnkNA2UsrZjCuZv9C"}
